   "text": "I read the structure as the cyclic peptide named under the drawing, H-Cpa-cyclo[D-Cys-Tyr-D-Aph(Val)-Lys-Thr-Cys]-D-Tyr-NH2, and wrote it as a SMILES with a disulfide ring closure between the two Cys sulfurs.\n\n**Residues, in chain order**\n1. N-terminal 4-chlorophenylalanine (Cpa), with a free amine. From the hashed NH2 bond I worked out S, i.e. the L form.\n2. D-Cys, whose side-chain sulfur forms the S\u2013S bond.\n3. L-Tyr.\n4. D-Aph(Val): D-4-aminophenylalanine whose aniline nitrogen is acylated by Val. From the hashed isopropyl bond I worked out S, i.e. L-Val.\n5. L-Lys, with a free \u03b5-amine.\n6. L-Thr.\n7. L-Cys, whose sulfur closes the disulfide to residue 2.\n8. C-terminal D-Tyr-NH2.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I took Cpa and Val from the wedges and hashes in the drawing. For the remaining residues I used the configurations given in the name rather than deriving each one from the drawing.\n\nSMILES: N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(Cl)cc1)C(=O)N[C@H](CS%10)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(O)cc1)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc1ccc(NC(=O)[C@@H](N)C(C)C)cc1)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CS%10)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc1ccc(O)cc1)C(N)=O"
